# games3 -- games that read their moves from standard input, fed enough to
# show them start and set their scene, 2026-09-14.  Only the fixed text is
# asserted: fish deals and wump places its hazards at random.  poker,
# blackjak, jotto and mastrm are NOT here: each re-asks forever once input
# runs out, and a head on the pipe does not stop them.

family  games3

case    advent-builds-its-database-and-scores-a-quit
run     /dd/CMDS/printf 'no\nquit\nyes\n' | /dd/CMDS/GAMES/advent
expect  Advent is ready.
expect  Welcome to adventure!!
expect  You scored 32 out of a possible 350 using 1 turns.

case    napoleon-opens-in-the-central-office
run     /dd/CMDS/printf 'q\n' | /dd/CMDS/GAMES/napoleon
expect  Napoleon, version 1.02, copyright (c) Pete Chown 1992
expect  The central office
expect  On the desk, there is a scroll.

case    fish-deals-a-hand
run     /dd/CMDS/printf 'n\n' | /dd/CMDS/GAMES/fish
expect  Would you like instructions (y or n)?
expect  Your hand is:

case    wump-sets-up-the-cave
run     /dd/CMDS/printf 'n\nq\nn\n' | /dd/CMDS/GAMES/wump
expect  You're in a cave with 20 rooms and 3 tunnels leading from each room.
expect  Move or shoot? (m-s)
